like so, and so first of all

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:42.679
I need to move it over 180 degrees. And I can do that really simply by

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:47.570
cutting straight through the Greenwich Meridian, which is 0.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:54.109
I'm gonna cut straight through here. Ok, so this is now going to go

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:58.190
180 degrees, which means I move this over here. And

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.890
I move this behind.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:07.099
But then we need to do a mirror image, which is really simple. If you've got transparencies,

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:13.070
you just turn it upside down. So there we go. So now we have the two maps

00:06:13.919 --> 00:06:17.059
flipped. And we can see here, there we had

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:24.589
Auckland, so Eden Park, and Eden Park is now over there. And it's - I've got it pretty spot on. So it's pretty close.

